0,Yaminawa language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yaminawa_language,"Yaminawa (Yaminahua) is a Panoan language of western Amazonia. It is spoken by the Yaminawá and some related peoples. Yaminawa constitutes an extensive dialect cluster. Attested dialects are two or more Brazilian Yaminawa dialects, Peruvian Yaminawa, Chaninawa, Chitonawa, Mastanawa (=Nastanawa), Parkenawa (= Yora or ""Nawa""), Shanenawa (Xaninaua, = Katukina de Feijó), Sharanawa (= Marinawa ...",Yaminahua,Panoan
1,Yaminawá - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yaminawá,"The Yaminawá translated to ""people of the axe."" They are also called the Iaminaua, Jaminawa, Yaminawá (in Brazil), and Yaminahua (in Peru and Bolívia), as well as Yuminahua, Yabinahua, Yambinahua, Yamanawa, and other variants. The Yaminawá name was given to them by outsiders. They have several autonyms including Bashonawá (basho = ""opossum""), Marinawá (mari = ""cutia"", an agouti ...",Yaminahua,Panoan
